\section{Comparing models responsibly}{

\itemize{
\item Use the same retained sample and response definition. Equal sample counts
do not establish sample identity, and criteria from different likelihood
definitions need not be comparable.
\item The existing guard warns for different row counts, and for default BIC
also different independent-unit counts. It does not compare row identities.
\item Check integration sensitivity and optimization before interpreting small
criterion differences. A higher-order fit need not be a more accurate fit.
\item Use likelihood-ratio tests only with the appropriate nesting, identified
parameters and boundary conditions; see \code{\link[=panel_select]{panel_select()}}.
}
